Package: zudiff
Title: Shortest Edit Scripts, Unified Diffs and Patches
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Pedro", "Baltazar", , "pedrobtz@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Computes the shortest edit script between two sequences
    (atomic vectors, raw vectors or the lines of two strings) and returns
    it as data, with Myers' algorithm (E. W. Myers (1986)
    <doi:10.1007/BF01840446>) or patience diff. Builds hunks with context,
    writes and parses unified diffs, and applies an edit script or a
    unified diff. Equality is that of match(), so missing values, signed
    zeros, encodings and factor labels compare as R users expect. The
    algorithms are written in the 'Goose' programming language
    (<https://github.com/aardappel/goose>) and compiled ahead of time to
    C, which the package bundles.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/pedrobtz/zudiff, https://pedrobtz.github.io/zudiff/
BugReports: https://github.com/pedrobtz/zudiff/issues
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1)
Suggests:
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
SystemRequirements: A C99 compiler. POSIX memory mapping and signals
    (mmap, mprotect, sigaction); Windows is not supported yet.
OS_type: unix
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Encoding: UTF-8
Language: en-GB
